{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"═══ START HERE — this ticket is CLAIMED, plan CERTIFIED, ready to implement ═══\n\nEverything needed is already in this ticket's comments. Do NOT re-investigate; five hypotheses are eliminated BY EXPERIMENT and re-testing them wastes the session.\n\n**DO THIS, IN ORDER (from the earlier comment 'IMPLEMENTATION ORDER, now fully determined'):**\n1. ContextVar in the workflow step executor carrying (step id, RAW declared token — `ctx.step['model']` for a prompt step, `batch['model_ladder'][0]` for a batch step). Set around each step, dropped on exit. Precedent: `_active_gate_config` at `llm/config.py:88`.\n2. `usage_log.record()` gains `step` + `model_class`, additive, following its existing `if model:` omission pattern. Write `model_class` ONLY when the raw token is in `CLASS_NAMES`.\n3. `runner.py:547` (the ONLY `record()` call site) passes both through from the ContextVar.\n4. THE RED TEST, at the seam that actually exercises resolution: real `RunnerAgentStep`, fake underlying runner injected via `get_runner(cfg, override=self._runner)` (`runs.py:236`), captured at `runner.run(req)` (`:261`) where **`req.config.model` is the POST-resolution value**. Assert per step under a class table whose values DIFFER from `cfg.model`. It must be RED first — today it reports `cfg.model` for every step.\n5. Re-run the live probe; the per-step attribution then names the broken wiring seam directly, and only then fix it (expect ONE of gate_dispatch / runs / batch_runner — do not change all three).\n\n**THE TRAP THAT WOULD MAKE A GREEN TEST WORTHLESS:** the existing offline harness (`tests/unit/workflow/test_code_review_workflow.py:402`) passes `agent_runner=_FakeRunner(...)`, which REPLACES `RunnerAgentStep` and therefore never runs `resolve_model(...)`. A recording runner built that way passes while proving only what 3768's tests already proved. The fake must sit BENEATH the production agent step, not instead of it.\n\n**WHY STEP 0 IS A PREREQUISITE AND NOT POLISH:** `RunRequest` carries no step id, and the prompt id cannot separate `base` from the `round_a`/`round_b` batch finder (all three use `code-review-base`). So neither the live usage log NOR the offline fake can attribute a call to a step without the ContextVar. That is the whole reason observability comes first.\n\nREMAINING SUSPECT (a suspect, not a conclusion): `config.py:211` resolves via `resolve_model_string(step or workflow or cfg.model)` with NO `repo_root`, while the live run executes inside `gate_source.gate_read_root(handle)`. Unverified, and it cannot be the whole story — a fallback class table would give `verify` SONNET and the log showed OPUS. Let step 5's data decide.\n\nWHEN b690 CLOSES: 3768's live-evidence criterion becomes satisfiable — re-run its probe, attest ON 3768 (the verifier reads only the ticket under test), and close it. That unblocks 0d76 -> eb6e -> 8625."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785616232560557001,"uuid":"66c0715f-4ed3-4ac0-bb79-b317950eb9aa"}